{"chunk_id": "595e35db2a2a", "text": "After cursing the celestial nymph Rambha in anger, Vishwamitra regrets that wrath has ruined the fruit of his austerities. Determined to conquer anger and desire completely, he undertakes an even harsher vow: a thousand years of silence, breath control, and extreme asceticism. When that period ends and he finally prepares to eat, Indra\u2014disguised as a brahmin\u2014begs for the food, and Vishwamitra gives it away without speaking. He resumes his penance for another thousand years, generating such intense spiritual power that smoke rises from his head and the cosmos begins to tremble. Alarmed, the gods beg Brahma to grant him brahmanhood. Brahma appears and proclaims Vishwamitra a Brahmarishi. At Vishwamitra\u2019s request, the sage Vasishta acknowledges him as such, resolving their long rivalry and completing Vishwamitra\u2019s transformation from king to supreme sage.\nAfter a thousand years of extreme austerities and restraint, Vishwamitra is finally recognized by Brahma and Vasistha as a Brahmarishi.\nThemes: ascetic perseverance, mastery over anger, recognition of spiritual status, divine approval, rivalry resolved", "vector": [0.006608183495700359, -0.03928534686565399, -0.0018103457987308502, -0.002660787431523204, -0.004459344781935215, 0.011047319509088993, -0.01554708182811737, -0.03354613110423088, -0.006581238470971584, -0.023495763540267944, 0.011795034632086754, 0.014092069119215012, 0.007227911148220301, 0.0035600662231445312, 0.003880034200847149, 0.004210106562823057, 0.05733828246593475, -0.007376106921583414, 0.017594877630472183, -0.01538541354238987, 0.0026961523108184338, -0.012300247326493263, -0.013889984227716923, 0.023509236052632332, -0.02791469171643257, -0.0025041713379323483, 0.01801251992583275, -0.024344520643353462, 0.0030817980878055096, -0.01721765287220478, 0.006756379269063473, 0.008346115238964558, 0.0022111479192972183, 0.004833202343434095, -0.029612205922603607, -0.004290940705686808, -